# Git Ignore Lab
## Commands Used
### Open project
```bash
cd GitDemo
```
### Create a log file
```bash
echo "Error Log" > error.log
```
### Create a log folder
```bash
mkdir log
``
### Create a file inside log folder
```bash
echo "Sample Log" > log/test.txt
```
### Create .gitignore file
```bash
touch .gitignore
```
or (Windows)
```bash
echo. > .gitignore
```
### Open .gitignore
```bash
notepad .gitignore
```
### Add the following lines
```text
*.log
log/
```
### Check repository status
```bash
git status
```
### Add .gitignore
```bash
git add .gitignore
```
### Commit
```bash
git commit -m "Added .gitignore"
```
### Push to GitHub
```bash
git push origin main
``
---
## Files Created
- welcome.txt
- error.log
- log/
- .gitignore
## Result
- All `.log` files are ignored.
- `log` folder is ignored.
- Only required files are tracked by Git.
